[
  {
    "sha": "62e162003f49512ed9088ca46e50674a76f6dd24",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDYyZTE2MjAwM2Y0OTUxMmVkOTA4OGNhNDZlNTA2NzRhNzZmNmRkMjQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T03:01:18Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T03:01:18Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(mcp): serve the MCP tool table live from inside the GUI\n\nAn opt-in server (--mcp-port <n> or CAMCRAFT_MCP_PORT; off by default)\nlistens on 127.0.0.1 only and carries the same newline-delimited JSON-RPC\n`camcraft-cli mcp` speaks on stdio. A listener thread moves lines to the\nUI thread over a channel (waking the idle loop with an empty winit user\nevent); the UI answers them in State::drain_actions through the new\napp::mcp::answer_live seam, which runs the existing tool dispatch against\nthe window's own world (a shared flecs handle) and History (lent for the\ncall). An agent's step is therefore an entry on the app's History: the\nbrowser shows it and Ctrl+Z undoes it like a user step. open_project is\nrefused in the live session (it would skip the unsaved-changes prompt).\n\n`camcraft-cli mcp --connect <host:port>` bridges stdio to the live\nsession for MCP clients that launch stdio servers. The status strip shows\n\"MCP listening on 127.0.0.1:<port>\" while the server runs; dropping the\ninbox at shutdown stops and joins the listener thread.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/mcp_live.rs (seam + undo, loopback socket,\nbridge, port flag) and the ui lib tests egui_app::tests::mcp_live.\nDecisions in docs/decisions/183-mcp-live-gui.md.\n\nFixes #183\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
