  {
    "sha": "c051ba9d08a8e9991ca644420daf1ca1c947bdd1",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGMwNTFiYTlkMDhhOGU5OTkxY2E2NDQ0MjBkYWYxY2ExYzk0N2JkZDE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T22:32:42Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T22:32:42Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(mcp): the live listener serves JSON-RPC lines only - a browser POST is refused\n\nReview of #474: any web page can POST to 127.0.0.1, and the listener\nread each line as JSON-RPC, so the HTTP headers failed but the body ran\n- a page could call save_project, post or export_tool_library with its\nown paths. Every non-blank line must now open a JSON object or array;\nanything else is refused (-32600) and the connection closed before a\nline reaches the app. Reads are bounded to the cap as they happen and\nwrites time out, so a client can neither grow memory nor stall the\nlistener.\n\nPinned by mcp_live::a_browser_post_never_reaches_the_app.\n\nRefs #183\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
