  {
    "sha": "c33f8f9ffe7bb2e0eef69eccc9c0492df5ed66de",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGMzM2Y4ZjlmZmU3YmIyZTBlZWY2OWVjY2M5YzA0OTJkZjVlZDY2ZGU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-09T22:46:42Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-09T22:46:42Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(mcp): an idle live-session client is dropped after a timeout\n\nThe live listener serves one client at a time; a local client that\nconnected and sent nothing held the session until it hung up. Now a\nclient that sends no complete line for the idle window (5 minutes by\ndefault; Inbox::listen_with_idle sets another, floored at the 50 ms\npoll step) gets an MCP notifications/message saying why, is closed,\nis logged by peer address (\"client <peer> dropped: idle ...\"), and the\nnext client is served. The clock resets after each answered line, so\nthe app's own answering time never counts. A newcomer does not\npre-empt a connected client before that.\n\nFixes #567\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
      "tree": {
